        "original_id": "7af2c429-594b-5748-b556-f3212297d9c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Carroll County, Ohio; Homewood Field; San Diego, California\n- People: Charles Carroll of Carrollton; Doc Watson\n- Topics: Declaration of Independence; Major League Baseball\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the last surviving signer of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Charles Carroll of Carrollton was the only Catholic signatory of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Carroll County, Ohio, is named for Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Homewood Field and the entire campus take their names from the estate of Charles Carroll of Carrollton.\n- Doc Watson, whose full name was Charles John Watson, was born on January 30, 1886, in Carroll County, Ohio.\n- Doc Watson was a pitcher in Major League Baseball.\n- Doc Watson died on December 30, 1949, in San Diego, California.",
